# Stock Scrapper

Stock Scrapper is a local Python application for collecting daily market data, storing it in SQLite, validating records, calculating a small set of transparent indicators, and generating CSV and HTML reports.

## What it does now

- Downloads daily historical price data with yfinance
- Stores data locally in SQLite
- Updates only missing data on later runs
- Validates new rows and records issues
- Calculates returns, moving averages, volatility, drawdown, and status flags
- Generates CSV and HTML reports

## What it does not do yet

- Machine learning
- News sentiment analysis
- Automatic trading
- Real-money brokerage integration
- Intraday data collection

## Project structure

- main.py: CLI entry point
- config/: settings and watchlist
- stock_scrapper/: application modules
- data/: database and local data directories
- reports/: generated reports
- logs/: log files
- tests/: pytest tests

## Windows setup

```powershell
py -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Running the app

```powershell
python main.py run
python main.py update
python main.py report
python main.py validate
python main.py status
```

## Watchlist

The watchlist is stored in config/watchlist.csv and can be edited with any text editor or spreadsheet tool.

## Database

The SQLite database is stored at data/market.db.

## Reports

CSV and HTML reports are written to the reports/ directory.

## Testing

```powershell
pytest
```

## Disclaimer

This project is for educational and research purposes only. It is not financial advice.
